# GDScript conventions

## Typing and style

- Statically type everything: variables, parameters, return values, and arrays (`Array[int]`). Use `:=` only when the type is obvious from the right-hand side.
- Follow the official Godot GDScript style guide. Files, functions, and variables are snake_case. `class_name` values and node names are PascalCase. Constants and enum members are CONSTANT_CASE. Private members start with an underscore.
- Name signals in the past tense (`player_joined`, `prop_grabbed`).
- Order each script as follows: `class_name` and `extends`, a `##` doc comment, signals, enums, constants, `@export` vars, public vars, private vars, `@onready` vars, built-in callbacks (`_init`, `_enter_tree`, `_ready`, `_process`, `_physics_process`, `_input`), public methods, private methods.
- Put a `##` doc comment on every public function and every exported or synced property.

## Structure

- Call down, signal up. A node may call methods on its children. To talk to a parent or a sibling scene, emit a signal or go through an autoload's public API.
- Reference nodes inside your own scene with `%UniqueName` (set `unique_name_in_owner`). Never reach into another scene's internals with a long `get_node()` path.
- Do not add a new autoload without a `docs/DECISIONS.md` entry. `Net` and `Campaign` are the planned ones.
- Keep scripts under roughly 300 lines. When one grows past that, split behavior into child component nodes with their own scripts.
- Gameplay and movement code goes in `_physics_process`. Read input through Input Map actions only, never hardcoded keys, and never the Command key.

## Values and paths

- Tuning numbers come from `Balance` (generated from the design workbook) or `Constants`. Never hardcode a balance value, and never edit `core/balance.gd` by hand. If a value you need doesn't exist yet, use a clearly named local constant, mark it `# TODO(balance): add to workbook`, and tell the developer.
- When code works around an open design question, name it in a comment, for example `# OQ-011: individual reset until decided`.
- File and folder names are lowercase snake_case, and every `res://` path must match the file's case exactly. Exported builds are case-sensitive even though macOS is not.

## Errors and logging

- Never ignore a returned `Error`. Check it, and `push_error()` with a useful message on failure.
- Use `assert()` for programmer mistakes, `push_warning()` for recoverable problems, and `push_error()` for failures.
- Prefix log lines with the system name, such as `print("[Net] peer %d joined" % id)`. Put noisy per-frame logging behind a debug flag so it is off by default.

## Comments

Comments should explain why something is done, not restate what the code does. When a choice exists because of networking (for example, a property is set only on the host), say so in the comment.
